4. PRIMARY BAND 500-12000 Hz: MEASURED FLOOR AND SIGNIFICANCE
==============================================================================
  14 carrier sub-bands, Welch nper=8192 -> modulation resolution 0.122 Hz.
  1565 non-mains bins searched in 3-200 Hz.

  WHY THE FLOOR IS LOCAL, NOT GLOBAL.  A first pass measured the floor in
  a single 230-480 Hz control band.  Against that floor the EMPTY ROOM
  showed 430 of 1614 bins above '5 sigma' -- the envelope spectrum is
  strongly coloured, so a floor measured elsewhere is simply the wrong
  floor.  A running median + running MAD with a guard band fixes it, and
  the empty-room false-alarm counts below are the proof that it is fixed.

