==============================================================================
5. DIRECT FAN-ON minus FAN-OFF TEST (signed, one-sided, unequal n handled)
==============================================================================
A fan detection requires fan-ON > fan-OFF.  The test is therefore SIGNED
and one-sided; an earlier unsigned version reported '4.23 sigma' at a bin
where fan-OFF was in fact the HIGHER of the two.

50 kSa/s matched pair, 7.5 s segments:
  n_on=16 segments, n_off=8 segments; 391 non-mains bins; nper=2048
  largest POSITIVE normal-equivalent sigma = 3.16 at 188.965 Hz (lag 5.3 ms, t=3.80, dof=16.2)
  3-sigma bins expected by chance 0.53, observed 1
  most negative sigma (fan-OFF higher) = -3.26 -- a two-sided sanity check:
  the distribution is symmetric about zero, i.e. pure noise.

100 kSa/s cross-check.  UNEQUAL DWELL: 25 s x2 fan-on vs 6 s fan-off.
Both are cut into 3 s segments so the per-segment estimator is IDENTICAL;
the unequal segment count then enters only through the Welch standard
error and the Welch-Satterthwaite dof, which deflates a 2-segment
reference to its true confidence.
  n_on=16  n_off=2 (only 2 -> dof about 15.0, not infinity)
  largest POSITIVE normal-equivalent sigma = 4.31 at 71.289 Hz (t=6.23, dof=15.0), 195 non-mains bins
  treating t as a z (dof=inf) would have read 6.23 -- the unequal-dwell correction is worth 1.92 sigma here.

==============================================================================
6. BLADE-FLASH HARMONIC-COMB SEARCH
==============================================================================
A blade flash is impulsive, so it should put power at f_bp AND its
harmonics.  Comb score = mean local-CFAR sigma over k*f0, k=1..4, scanned
across the whole blade-pass hypothesis space 10-150 Hz.

  Comb hypotheses rejected because some harmonic k*f0 lands on mains: 102 of 1147 (this is what removed the spurious f0=30 Hz, whose 2nd harmonic IS 60 Hz).
  fanON_50k_a  : best NON-MAINS comb f0 =  91.055 Hz, score  1.83 sigma | RPM N=3/4/5: 1821/1366/1093
  fanON_50k_b  : best NON-MAINS comb f0 =  58.950 Hz, score  1.82 sigma | RPM N=3/4/5: 1179/884/707
  fanOFF_50k   : best NON-MAINS comb f0 =  61.514 Hz, score  1.43 sigma | RPM N=3/4/5: 1230/923/738

  The empty room scores as high as the fan-on room -> no fan-specific comb.

==============================================================================
7. ENVELOPE AUTOCORRELATION (the assigned primary statistic)
==============================================================================
  Band 500-12000 Hz, carrier mains notch +/-5 Hz, envelope at 4000 Hz (lag resolution 0.25 ms).
  The mains comb is ALSO removed in the envelope domain, so a 16.7 ms lag
  cannot survive as a disguised blade period.
  Blade-pass lag window 6.7-100 ms.

    fanON_50k_a   mains notched + mains LAGS excluded: peak +0.0490 at  10.80 ms ( 92.59 Hz)  tail sd 0.0090 ->  5.42 sigma
                  no notch, no exclusion:             peak +0.2435 at  16.56 ms ( 60.39 Hz)  <- the mains period, identical fan ON
    fanON_50k_b   mains notched + mains LAGS excluded: peak +0.0413 at  10.08 ms ( 99.21 Hz)  tail sd 0.0073 ->  5.68 sigma
                  no notch, no exclusion:             peak +0.2033 at  16.56 ms ( 60.39 Hz)  <- the mains period, identical fan ON
    fanOFF_50k    mains notched + mains LAGS excluded: peak +0.0358 at  11.52 ms ( 86.81 Hz)  tail sd 0.0070 ->  5.10 sigma
                  no notch, no exclusion:             peak +0.1854 at  16.56 ms ( 60.39 Hz)  <- the mains period, present with the fan OFF too

  Fan-ON and fan-OFF autocorrelations are the same height at the same lag.
  Fan-ON minus fan-OFF ACF peak = +0.0132 against a MEASURED fan-OFF tail sd of 0.0070 = 1.88 sigma.

==============================================================================
8. FMCW CROSS-CHECK on the fan (identical config to the positive control)
==============================================================================
  MTI-envelope energy 1.0-2.5 m: fan_on -28.16 dB, empty room -27.24 dB, difference -0.92 dB.  The person was +6.77 dB.
  fan_on cadence-band periodicity peak 2.93 Hz at 2.99 sigma (empty-room reference 1.20 sigma) -> below the 5-sigma bar.
  2.93 Hz would imply 59 RPM with 3 blades -- not a running fan.
  The fan is 2.5 m away, inside the range gate that showed the person at
  +6.8 dB.  It returns LESS than the empty room.

==============================================================================
9. SENSITIVITY - what blade AM depth WOULD this pipeline have caught?
==============================================================================
  AM depth  5.00% of the IF ->    32.33 sigma recovered
  AM depth  3.00% of the IF ->    11.10 sigma recovered
  AM depth  2.00% of the IF ->     4.86 sigma recovered
  AM depth  1.00% of the IF ->     1.00 sigma recovered
  AM depth  0.50% of the IF ->     0.04 sigma recovered

  5-sigma detection threshold of this pipeline on this 60 s record:
  AM depth ~3.00% of the IF.  A blade flash shallower than that is invisible here.
  With the IF on 4-5 ADC codes and AC rms at 0.47 LSB, the quantiser, not
  the algorithm, sets this wall.

